As a PAM Engineer,
I want to research and create a documented approach to onboard and manage and Database owned Active Directory Service Accounts (SQL and Oracle, Mongo DB, and Post Crest) within CyberArk,
So that the organization has a standardized, secure, and repeatable process for privileged account onboarding and lifecycle management for database owned AD SVS Account platforms, reducing operational risk and ensuring compliance with PAM governance standards.
Business Justification:
Database owned Active Directory SVS accounts (SQL and Oracle) represent a portion of privileged access within the enterprise. Without a defined onboarding and management approach within CyberArk, these accounts remain outside of PAM governance, increasing the risk of unauthorized access, credential exposure, and audit findings. Establishing a research-backed approach will enable consistent onboarding, password management, and session monitoring for these account types.


Acceptance Criteria
AC1: Platform research across all four DBs (SQL Server, Oracle, MongoDB, PostgreSQL) covering discovery methods, CPM plugins, platform configs, and connection components.
AC2: Confluence approach document with strategy, platform selection, naming conventions, and CPM policy.
AC3: Prerequisites and dependencies identified.
AC4: Lifecycle management (rotation, session monitoring, governance compliance).
AC5: Stakeholder review and approval.


Document this and place in word document
Facts: safe naming should be IN-LOCAL-{PostGreSQL/SQL/ORA}

Platform will be defined for each DB service
